Z||000000||1FST2M6||01-27-2000||02:01 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/emission.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/emission.jpg</A>  <BR>Ok just FYI. here are the scans of my last Emissions inspection. As you can see the EGR DOES work its little butt off doing what its supposed to...  Sorry i couldn't make it a smaller file.. my new computer is still beating me at everything I try to do.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||01-27-2000||02:13 PM||||I've always been for keeping my EGR connected. But I had no idea the system did that much. Wow! Looks like we have proof that the EGR does actually do something.||||reg||1
Z||000002||dogtired||01-27-2000||02:26 PM||||Great Info, often thought about blocking mine off? (but don't really want to)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>RPM control or lack thereof seems to be one of my biggest problems on both my V6s, could be TPS Could be Vaccuum leak, Could be EGR tube???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>I see a big difference in RPM on your chart? Did the EGR do that too??<BR>Great Info, THANKS||||reg||6
