Z||000004||1FST2M6||01-27-2000||04:22 PM||||Sorry about the monsterous file size.. I got a new computer and can't find a real pic viewer with "resize to fit screen" I have to try and figure it out through Photoshop 5.5 . As for the RPM thats was different cause of the drivers. On Tester on one day another on the other... but the guys at the Emissions center said the RPMs wouldn't matter as long as there is a load on the motor and part throttle. So the EGR would work. As for the Idle lope I had the same proplem a few days after I bought my car.. I invested $10 in new vacuum hose and spen all day saturday replacing them... the lope went away and hasn't returned. Just make sure if you use silicon hose (not rubber) that you attach ALL the hoses to their proper place with a plastic Zip tie.. the hose will get warm and shake off.. Glad it was easy to get to the first time... Silicon maybe pretty but stick with rubber.. it's cheaper and STAYS where you put it!    ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||01-27-2000||07:03 PM||||That is excellent data!  Hard to argue with the extent of change induced by the EGR on those values.  I would hope that those who have considered EGR system disconnection will see this and possibly save themselves the costs of an engine rebuild.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||01-28-2000||09:38 AM||||My 88 Formula has a chip that disables EGR, has no CAT-conv, a Crane Compucam and passed Florida emmision test last year. Don't know how. At least the tester should had a broken mirror (to check cat) or could not differentiate between a cat and a sherry bomb...||||reg||6
Z||000007||1FST2M6||01-28-2000||10:41 AM||||Yeah you can pass emissions just fine, the motors do run very clean.. but the shape of the combustion chambers and the timing make the combustion temps STUPID high and thats why I failed. Does Fl. check for NOx (Oxides of Nitrogen)? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||01-28-2000||01:35 PM||||The EGR snaps closed at WOT too. Only opens on mild to moderate throttle at cruise. Since the AFR is increased at WOT, the cylinder temps drop with the EGR cold. Well, they don't rise as much.<P>Has anybody checked to see if the EGR is negative or positive backpressure?<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||01-28-2000||02:49 PM||||According to the Mitchel on Demand software at the shop it is a Negative back pressure device. (whats the difference?) yes, the egr slams shut at WOT, but at the temperatures that can make the readings I had are on the verge of melting a piston. And unfortunatly even I can't drive FULL-TILT-BOOGY all the time. the part throttle is what kills the car. Also with the injectors i have with the EGR connected she spits,sputters and blows smoke after driving anymore than maybe a mile, mile and a half cause it loads up on fuel and can't burn it all... unplug said EGR and POOF fast car again.. but only wide open and with the nitrous running.. but thats a sacrifice i had to make... fast on the bottle or off... reliable or on the edge of total destruction. Since i have a spare motor... i'll kill this one now and tell everyone how not to kill theirs. Just wish the spare was an 8 in stead of a mild 2.8... oh well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> uuum totaly lost my point..  ok..   Brain Flake...   ||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||01-28-2000||04:21 PM||||The EGR could be floating open on high backpressures in the exhaust system. We have to talk in terms of everything working correctly. The Fiero's sister engine uses N and P EGR's depending on auto or manual.<P>I think the TPS% levels are 9% off and 6% on, but again, the backpressure could open it.<P>Should I check this or does it really matter? I think I'm drifting off subject. Damn multi-verses!<P><BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||01-28-2000||04:28 PM||||Seems like I remember something in the shop manual about there being 3 kinds of EGRs; Positive, Negative and Ported. The V6 is Ported, the EGR solenoid cycles on and off to get the correct amount of recirculation. The L4 is either Positive or Negative, can't remember which.<P>||||reg||1
